Specimens in a project that uses the `Paleontology` catalog format show the
fossil attribute form. Sex and weight units work the same way in every taxon
group; see [Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/).

{% aside type="danger" %}

Paleontology support is in development and is not yet available in released
versions of NAHPU. Track progress in the
[`dev` branch](https://github.com/nahpu/nahpu/tree/dev). Fields and this page may
change before release.

{% /aside %}

## Fossil attributes

- `Fossil type`: the kind of fossil, such as a body fossil or trace fossil.
- `Sex`: select from the configured specimen-sex vocabulary.
- `Ontogenetic stage`: the developmental stage of the individual.
- `Weight`: the specimen weight, with a selectable unit.
- `Specimen description`: a free-text description of the specimen.
- `Remarks`: additional notes.

## Sites

Paleontology projects replace the site habitat form with depositional
environment fields: `Depositional Environment Type`,
`Depositional Environment Subtype`, `Standard Preservation Type`, and
`Comments on sedimentology and paleoenvironment`. See
[Sites](/en/usages/sites/).
